#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/jordan.rst:12
msgid "Legal framework for e-invoicing in Jordan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/jordan.rst:14
msgid ""
"In Jordan, businesses must comply with `electronic invoicing regulations "
"<https://istd.gov.jo/EN/List/Electronic_billing_User_Manual>`_ established "
"by the `Income and Sales Tax Department (ISTD) <https://istd.gov.jo/En/List/"
"Laws>`_ through the Jordanian National Electronic Invoicing System, commonly "
"referred to as JoFotara. The system requires businesses within the mandated "
"scope to issue and submit electronic invoices and related debit and credit "
"notes through the JoFotara platform in accordance with the government’s "
"technical and legal requirements. Businesses must generate invoices in the "
"required UBL 2.1 format and submit them for real-time validation through the "
"JoFotara platform. Upon successful validation, invoices receive a QR code "
"used for verification and compliance purposes. Depending on the taxpayer "
"type and applicable tax regime, invoices may require percentage-based taxes, "
"fixed taxes, or both. The framework aims to improve tax compliance, "
"transparency, and digitalization across Jordan’s tax system."
msgstr ""

